From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Qianhui Xu <xiaqinghuan@mail.ustc.edu.cn>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750-lenovo-elden: add flash LED NTC
 thermal zone

The stock firmware has a dedicated NTC next to the flash LED: a pmk8550
VADC channel on sid 1 / AMUX2 with a 100k pull-up (reg 0x145), plus a
"flash-led-ntc" thermal zone that the stock thermal HAL watches (it is
listed in the vendor sensor-listener-names).  The mainline board file
exposes neither, so the NTC is unreadable and the flash LED temperature
cannot be observed.

This is a monitoring gap, not a safety gap: upstream leds-qcom-flash does
its own real-time current derating from the PMIC THERM_THRSH1/2 and
STATUS2 registers, so the zone is added for observation only, with a
single passive trip at the stock threshold (125 C) and no cooling device.

The zone node name must match the thermal-zones schema pattern (node
names of the form "<name>-thermal"), hence "flash-ntc-thermal" rather than
the stock "flash-led-ntc"; only the label of the trip point keeps the
stock spelling.

Gate (build/daily tip 4bdf1711b5, this patch applied):
  make -j26 ARCH=arm64 CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu- CHECK_DTBS=1 \
       qcom/sm8750-lenovo-elden.dtb
  -> DTC [C] sm8750-lenovo-elden.dtb, rc=0, 0 diagnostics
  -> 153129 B (tip) -> 153488 B (+359 B)
On-device readback still pending; the 0x145 sid/channel mapping is copied
from stock and unverified.

Signed-off-by: Qianhui Xu <xiaqinghuan@mail.ustc.edu.cn>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-elden.dts | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-elden.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-elden.dts
index 9f196da964..331198faff 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-elden.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-elden.dts
@@ -26,6 +26,27 @@ / {
 
 	/* Stock CPU/GPU thermal HAL junction limit: 105 C, 5 C hysteresis. */
 	thermal-zones {
+		/*
+		 * Stock has a dedicated NTC next to the flash LED (pmk8550 VADC
+		 * AMUX2, pre-scaled 100k pull-up).  Upstream leds-qcom-flash does
+		 * its own real-time derating from the PMIC THERM_THRSH/STATUS
+		 * registers, so this zone is for monitoring only, not for safety.
+		 */
+		flash-ntc-thermal {
+			polling-delay-passive = <0>;
+			polling-delay = <0>;
+
+			thermal-sensors = <&pmk8550_vadc 0x145>;
+
+			trips {
+				flash_led_ntc_passive: trip-passive {
+					temperature = <125000>;
+					hysteresis = <1000>;
+					type = "passive";
+				};
+			};
+		};
+
 		/*
 		 * Graded passive cooling (recalibrated 2026-10-02).
 		 * State == cpufreq/devfreq cdev level (higher = lower freq).
@@ -3176,3 +3197,14 @@ wcd_tx: codec@0,3 {
 		qcom,tx-port-mapping = <2 2 3 4>;
 	};
 };
+
+&pmk8550_vadc {
+	/* Flash LED NTC, same channel (sid 1 / AMUX2 100k PU) the stock DTS uses. */
+	channel@145 {
+		reg = <0x145>;
+		label = "pm8550_flash_led_ntc";
+		qcom,ratiometric;
+		qcom,hw-settle-time = <200>;
+		qcom,pre-scaling = <1 1>;
+	};
+};
